    fix: AUG-070 concurrent answer writers re-mint on id collision instead of refusing
    
    The race (DO-7 evidence: 2 writers x 30 answers into one namespace, 18 refusals,
    102 decision rows for 101 logical answers, 9 duplicate option ids, one id rendered
    twice by dump --config with two different real choices): DuckBrain enforces NO
    uniqueness — referential integrity is ours — so the mint->check->insert window
    races two ways.
    
      (a) writer B mints the id A already stored -> B's node_exists check fires ->
          B EXITS rc=1 and the ANSWER IS LOST (the dominant observed shape);
      (b) both writers' checks pass before either insert lands -> duplicate id rows.
    
    Fix, auger.py (additive; cmd_answer structure otherwise untouched):
    
      1. AUTO-MINTED path (no --id): the duplicate check is a BOUNDED RE-MINT loop
         (AUG070_ID_ATTEMPTS = 3 attempts). Each attempt re-mints from the live
         highest id via the same page-safe next_id read (AUG-069 semantics and the
         three-digit decision width untouched) and re-checks; the loop exits to the
         normal write path the moment the id is free. After the bound it refuses
         loudly naming the id and the attempt count — the mint may not spin on a
         store that answers "taken" forever — and the refusal is proven to write
         NOTHING (test asserts zero POSTs).
      2. EXPLICIT --id path: terminal refusal kept, message now states the guarantee:
         NOTHING was stored (no decision, no options, no evidence, no edges), and
         that the auto-minted path re-mints instead of refusing.
      3. Residual insert-insert window (shape b, optional req 5 taken): on the
         auto-minted path the decision is read back bounded (id=eq.<did>&limit=2)
         after the insert — one row is ours, two is ours plus a sibling's. On
         detection a WARNING: DUPLICATE IDS line is printed naming the id and count.
         Nothing is deleted; the residue is left for a human dedupe decision.
      4. dump self-check: duplicate decision ids and duplicate option ids are
         surfaced as a named warning block ("WARNING: DUPLICATE IDS: D-074 x2,
         D-074-O1 x3 — concurrent writers collided; dedupe before trusting this
         config") and the render CONTINUES — a drifted record is still worth
         reading (the AUG-015 doctrine); what it no longer does is render one id
         as two different real choices with no signal. New pure helper
         duplicate_id_warning_lines() beside activation_warning_lines().
    
    All reads/writes stay on the existing db()/select()/insert()/insert_decision()
    transport (429 backpressure property untouched); no hand-rolled HTTP.
    
    Tests (tests/test_auger.py, fake transport at db(), RaceServer extends the
    established StandInServer pattern with POSTs and two race shapes):
    
      * test_a_lost_race_remints_and_lands_the_answer_under_a_new_id — ghost row
        appears on the id=eq.D-074 check read (shape a): asserts re-mint to D-075,
        exactly one decision POST, the answer landed under the NEW id with the new
        evidence_key, the ghost row untouched, no dead-attempt option ids stored.
      * test_a_permanently_contended_answer_is_bounded_and_names_the_id_and_attempts
        — highest id frozen, every check says taken: asserts the refusal names the
        id and "re-checked 3 times", and that zero POSTs were written.
      * test_an_explicit_duplicate_id_refusal_says_nothing_was_stored — the --id
        refusal message states NOTHING was stored and names the auto-minted path.
      * test_dump_names_duplicate_ids_rather_than_rendering_them_silently —
        duplicated decision/option rows seeded via the fake: asserts the named
        DUPLICATE IDS warning, that the render continues (both rows readable),
        rc 0.
    
